From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:45:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 18/66] qualcommax: ipq807x: c-230: light the radio LEDs

The 2.4, 5 and WLAN LEDs had no trigger. Phy numbers follow the order the
radios were first found in, and they differ between units, as on the Arista
C-260. So board.d cannot name them. A hotplug script ties each LED to its
radio by device path instead, with the radio's phyNradio trigger: the LED
is lit while the radio is enabled.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 .../hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-230-leds  | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-230-leds

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-230-leds b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-230-leds
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..8fb21bc79e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/ipq807x/base-files/etc/hotplug.d/ieee80211/12-arista-c-230-leds
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Arista C-230: each radio LED follows its radio, found by device path.
+# Phy numbers follow the order the radios were first found in, which
+# differs between units. 2.4 and 5 are the IPQ8074's radios, WLAN is the
+# QCA9882 on pcie0. "phyNradio" lights the LED while the radio is enabled.
+
+[ "$ACTION" = add ] || exit 0
+
+. /lib/functions.sh
+
+[ "$(board_name)" = arista,c-230 ] || exit 0
+
+case "$(readlink "/sys/class/ieee80211/$DEVICENAME/device")" in
+*/c000000.wifi)
+	if iw phy "$DEVICENAME" info | grep -q "Band 1:"; then
+		led=green:wlan-2ghz
+	else
+		led=green:wlan-5ghz
+	fi
+	;;
+*/0000:01:00.0)
+	led=green:wlan
+	;;
+*)
+	exit 0
+	;;
+esac
+
+echo "${DEVICENAME}radio" > "/sys/class/leds/$led/trigger"
